%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: ToIvarsteadSerious
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ({mc}'s been pretty quiet so far...)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (...)
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852487
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Hey, {mc}?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: Huh-?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Sorry for zoning out, what's up?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, about that Ancano guy-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852488
    - rid: 9079475250346852489
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: You said he was a Thalmor, what does that mean?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852491
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Ah, well...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852492
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: That's a very loaded question; one that a lot of the current politics
      of Tamriel revolves around.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you want the whole history lesson, or just the "what does that even
      mean" part?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I'd like to know as much as possible, so the history lesson, I guess.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852493
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Alright, so the current year is 201 of the fourth era.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's been six eras, the Dawn, the Merethic, and then first through
      fourth.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852494
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: As far as the Thalmor are concerned, it's important to know specifically
      how the third era started and ended.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Towards the end of the second era, the High Elves of the Shimmering Isles
      and the Wood Elves of Valenwood formed the second Aldmeri Dominion.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: There's a lot to unpack there...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Just know that elves prefer to be ruled by elves and have a general disdain
      for the races of man.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Mostly because elves consider themselves to be direct descendents of
      the ancient spirits who created this world-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And through creation were basically duped into mortality.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Anyway, the Aldmeri Dominion is sort of a political symbol of elven unity
      against the barbarity of man.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Now, the second era was ended with the founding of the Third Empire of
      Cyrodiil; an empire ruled by men.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852499
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The founding emperor, Tiber Septim, basically used a giant golem with
      borderline divine power to conquer the entire continent-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Which includes the elves of the Aldmeri Dominion.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, for the elves, the start of the third era is marked by a humiliating
      defeat from their lessers.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Now, the third era ends with the dynasty of the original emperor, Tiber
      Septim.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And it ended the way any good dynasty does-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: World-ending apocalypse.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852502
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'So, to give as brief a rundown on the Oblivion Crisis, which ended the
      third era, as possible:'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852503
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Mehrunes Dagon, a Daedric Prince (which were the most powerful ancient
      spirits or gods that chose to not create the mortal realm) decides to invade
      Tamriel.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: All hell breaks loose, somewhat literally.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Havoc is wrought all across the continent until the last heir of the
      Septim dynasty basically sacrifices his lineage to stop the invasion.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The invasion is stopped, the mortal realm saved, but the Empire is leaderless
      and troubled.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, certain prejudiced elves in the Summerset Isles, the Thalmor, decide
      to take credit for stopping the Oblivion Crisis.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: And since the Empire's in chaos, the Thalmor could spin any claim to
      the contrary as Imperial propaganda.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: The Thalmor use this goodwill that they gained from this lie to get positions
      of power in elven society.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Overtime, they grow bolder and bolder as the Empire weakens, until they
      secede entirely, taking Valenwood and Elsywer with them.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So, the Oblivion Crisis gave the most racist and evil elves the most
      power in their society.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: So... the Thalmor are Elf-Nazis?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852496
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Pretty much, yeah.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852497
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: It's a shame Yuri wasn't here for this, ahaha~
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852498
    - rid: 9079475250346852501
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, she's been pretty chatty about all things lore.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852504
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: 'It''s almost as if she doesn''t really get the chance to do that too
      often, heh. '
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852505
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: She really doesn't, no...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852506
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Has she tried talking about that stuff in the literature club?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852507
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Not really, no.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852508
    - rid: 9079475250346852509
    - rid: 9079475250346852510
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I'd say she had one too many argument with Natsuki early on about what
      counted as literature, and just...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Sort of gave up on sharing after that.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852511
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: I feel like our conversation had a major tone shift!
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean, in her defense, it's not like Sayori's the type of person who'd
      be able to do anything other than nod along...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852512
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Which based off of our previous conversations, I assume you've experienced
      before?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852513
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, yeah...?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: What are you getting at, Monika?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: That-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852514
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852515
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: That I feel like I didn't do a good enough job as president for her.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852516
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I mean, the literature club is supposed to be a place for everybody-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: But I couldn't give one of my members a safe enough place to discuss
      her literature.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852517
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Hell, <i>you're</i> the one that actually called her to talk about the
      book the two of you were reading...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852518
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Uh, Monika, how'd you know about that?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852519
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I overheard you when you shared your Chaos account with her, ahaha!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852520
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh. Fair enough.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852521
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: What do you want me to say?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Hmm?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852522
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You've been talking about how you felt like you failed Yuri, and how
      you felt like I succeeded in comparison...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So what do you want from me?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Help? Validation?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Verbal prostration?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852523
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Do you even know what that means, {mc}?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, physical prostration would be putting your head to the floor while
      kneeling, as a sign of self-diminishment-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: So verbal prostration would be me saying mean words that make you feel
      like you're prostrating yourself.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... you've got quite the vocabulary, {mc}.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852524
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, I have to do my best as a representative of a literature club-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: But you're dodging my question, Monika. What do you want?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852525
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852526
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Nothing, really.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852527
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I just wanted to get that stuff off of my chest, with someone who'd listen.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: ... alright.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You plan on doing better?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852528
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, it sounds like this stuff's been eating at you, so how are you
      going to do better?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You gonna ask Yuri about her books, or something?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ... I don't know...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852529
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Well, Monika, if you really feel bad about it, and really want to change-
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: You have to be deliberate about it.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Because it's really easy to be a creature of habit, and fall back into
      negative tendencies just because that's what you usually do.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: ...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852530
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: You're right, {mc}.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852531
    - rid: 9079475250346852532
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Sorry for pausing our journey just to talk about my troubles, ahaha!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852533
    - rid: 9079475250346852534
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Huh?
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: ... I've only now noticed that we've just been standing on this bridge
      next to a waterfall for a while now.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: We were walking and talking just fine when <i>I</i> was monologuing...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852537
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Maybe you should work on that too while you're thinking about self-help,
      Monika.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852538
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh come on, why can't a girl lay out her every flaw resting by a waterfall?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852536
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: It's simply the most romantic place to do it!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852535
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, so Sayori really did misread this whole situation!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852539
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 905407d7a8ed6004ebfd47e9529ecf8c, type: 2}
    dialog: <i>You</i> were the one looking for an excuse to spend time with <i>me</i>!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852540
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, keep telling yourself that, {mc}...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852541
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 9079475250346852542
